<article class="env-lemma" id="02J3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02J3">Lemma <span data-tag="02J3">29.16.5</span>.</a> Let $f : T \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. If $f$ is locally of finite type, then $f(T_{\text{ft-pts}}) \subset S_{\text{ft-pts}}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $T$ is the spectrum of a field this is Lemma <a href="/tag/01TA" data-tag="01TA">29.16.1</a>. In general it follows since the composition of morphisms locally of finite type is locally of finite type (Lemma <a href="/tag/01T3" data-tag="01T3">29.15.3</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>